Perform five maneuvers to assess the "SITS" muscles of the _rotator cuff_ and the bicipital tendon.

## Five Maneuvers for SITS Muscle Assessment

### Strength Tests

* _External rotation lag test (Fig. 16-7)._ With the patient's arm flexed to go degrees with palm up, rotate the arm into full external rotation.
* _Internal rotation lag test (Fig. 16-8)._ Ask the patient to place the dorsum of the hand on the low back with the elbow flexed to go degrees. Then you lift the hand off the back, which further internally rotates the shoulder. Ask the patient to keep the hand in this position.
* _Drop-arm test (Fig. 16-9)._ Ask the patient to fully abduct the arm to shoulder level, up to go degrees, and lower it slowly. Note that abduction above shoulder level, from go to 120 degrees, reflects action of the deltoid muscle.

### Composite Test

_External rotation resistance test (Fig. 16-10)._ Ask the patient to adduct and flex the arm to go degrees, with the thumbs turned up. Stabilize the elbow with one hand and apply pressure proximal to the patient's wrist as the patient presses the wrist outward in external rotation.